\paragraph{Simulation dataset.}
Simulation records use \texttt{oceanography-waves-lib} release
\texttt{v1.2.1}, archive \texttt{sim-data-files-vessel-rao-28ft.zip}.
Motion and IMU channels describe the centre of gravity of an estimated
28 ft (8.53 m) fin-keel sailboat at zero forward speed and fixed heading.
The analytical response-amplitude operators (RAOs) include surge, sway,
heave, roll and pitch; Euler yaw is held fixed. These are estimated
coefficients, not measured hull-specific RAOs. File heights and periods
identify the incident sea, and spectrum CSVs remain incident-wave spectra;
they are not vessel-motion spectra. JONSWAP and PM records drive the RAOs
with their first-order incident components, without particle Stokes drift
or higher-order particle harmonics. Regular-wave elevation harmonics are
filtered by the same response. The largest cases are extrapolated stress
tests. The default IMU is at the centre of gravity; lever-arm studies add
an explicit sensor offset. The wave-theory derivations and auxiliary
Fenton surface plots describe incident waves separately from vessel motion.
